"Taiwan is connected to the world by 14 international undersea cables, which come ashore at landing stations in places like Tamsui and Toucheng. Because there are many cables and many routes, the internet can keep working when one breaks. In 2023, when both cables to the Matsu Islands were cut by passing ships, the islands had very slow internet until they were repaired. That is why engineers keep building more paths: the internet works because no single road is the only road.": "052600f780f9",
